### Page 1 of 4

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: " A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING SUBMISSION OF AN APPLICATION
TO THE WYOMING STATE LOAN AND INVESTMENT BOARD FOR A
LOAN
FROM
THE
WYOMING
DRINKING
WATER
STATE
REVOLVING FUND FOR THE HYPOCHLORITE GENERATION
PROJECT IN THE AMOUNT OF FOUR MILLION DOLLARS AND
AUTHORIZING THE DIRECTOR OF THE BOARD OF PUBLIC
UTILITIES TO EXECUTE THE APPLICATION AND ALL RELATED
DOCUMENTS."

WHEREAS, Wyoming Statute 15-7-401, provides for a Board of Public Utilities (the
"Board") to manage, operate, maintain and control municipal waterworks, sanitary sewer system
and sewage disposal plants;

WHEREAS, in accordance with state statute, Section 2.68.010 of the city code established
the Board to have exclusive authority to manage, operate, maintain and control the Cheyenne
Municipal Waterworks, Sanitary Sewage System and Sewage Disposal Plants of the City and to
make all rules and regulations necessary for the safe, economical and efficient operation and
maintenance of the above facilities;

WHEREAS, the existing chlorine gas disinfection system at the RL Sherard Water
Treatment Plant (the "WTP") uses chemicals that would be hazardous to staff and adjacent
properties in the event of a leak, and are subject to volatile chemical and transportation costs;

WHEREAS, the Board desires to pursue the Hypochlorite Generation project (the
"Project") to replace the existing chlorine gas disinfection process at the WTP with an onsite
sodium hypochlorite generation system;

WHEREAS, the Project cost estimate for equipment procurement and construction costs is
approximately five million dollars ($5,000,000.00);

WHEREAS, the Project has been awarded a one million dollar ($1,000,000.00) American
Rescue Plan Act grant;

WHEREAS, a four million dollar ($4,000,000.00) loan from the Wyoming Drinking Water
State Revolving Fund is subject to a loan origination fee of five-tenths percent (0.5%), which is
estimated to amount to twenty thousand dollars ($20,000.00);

WHEREAS, the Board and the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne recognizes that
the annual principal and interest payment on the proposed loan will be approximately two hundred
thirty-two thousand nine hundred eighty-two dollars and ninety-four cents ($232,982.94);

WHEREAS, the Board and the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne are committed to
repaying the loan from revenue from the Water Enterprise Fund; and

5:20 pm, Jul 16, 2024
```

### Page 2 of 4

```text
Page 2 of 2
WHEREAS, the Board recognizes that the Project is necessary to increase resiliency in
water treatment, improve public safety related to storing and handling chlorine gas, reduce
greenhouse gas emissions with fewer truck deliveries to the WTP, and utilize the renewable energy
source from the hydropower generator located at the WTP.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Board of Public Utilities may submit an application on
behalf of the City of Cheyenne to the Wyoming State Loan and Investment Board for a loan from
the Wyoming Drinking Water State Revolving Fund for an amount not to exceed four million
dollars ($4,000,000) for Project costs such as, but not limited to, engineering services,
construction, administration, and all related costs of the Hypochlorite Generation Project; and

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the Mayor, the City Clerk, and the Director of the
Board of Public Utilities are hereby designated as the authorized representatives of the City of
Cheyenne to act on behalf of the City of Cheyenne in all matters related to this application and
related documents, including any amendments to the Project Agreement.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2024.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
```

